.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fIlibmpq\fP library creates and reads MPQ archives, decrypts and
decompresses file data, and extracts files compressed with zlib, bzip2, or
PKWARE implosion. Creation uses seekable v1 or v2 archives and may be driven
through a streaming writer or buffer/path convenience functions. The current
writer supports raw sectors, encrypted tables and payloads, generated
listfiles, and zlib or bzip2 multi-compression.
.PP
An archive handle is not safe for concurrent operations. Use
\fBlibmpq__archive_clone\fP() to create one independent reader per worker.
Cloning reopens the original backing path and reparses its metadata; it is
not snapshot semantics. The path must remain readable and unchanged while
clones are created or used.
